WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.170
Every Christmas, businesses
compete for attention.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.070
Discounts.

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:07.930
Promotions.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.890
Advertisements.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.290
But what if, this year, Shawarma
Moods did something different?

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.250
Something that doesn't just sell a
meal, but brings people together.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.310
Here's the idea.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.130
A customer buys two shawarmas.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.290
They pay for both.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.630
They enjoy one, fresh and crispy.

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.600
And the second one is set aside for someone
in our community who needs a warm meal

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.640
this Christmas.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:43.830
One for you.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.230
One for someone in need.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.350
Buy one.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.140
Give one.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.950
Then Shawarma Moods steps in too.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:03.380
For every verified donated shawarma, the
restaurant adds one extra dollar to a

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.130
separate community kitchen fund.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.710
Customers fund the meals.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.670
The restaurant adds its own commitment.

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:16.500
Reach one thousand donated meals, and
that's one thousand dollars from Shawarma

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:17.540
Moods.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.510
The challenge: one thousand meals.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.870
A simple tracker shows every milestone.

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.453
Two hundred and fifty.

00:01:35.493 --> 00:01:36.730
Five hundred.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:39.283
Seven hundred and fifty.

00:01:39.323 --> 00:01:40.850
One thousand.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:45.710
In a live campaign, it would
count verified donations only.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:50.820
And if capacity and budget are approved,
a stretch goal of two thousand could

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:51.860
follow.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.790
This isn't about guilt, and
it isn't about charity photos.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.130
It's about making generosity easy.

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:07.790
Grab lunch with a friend,
add one for someone else,

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:09.590
and watch the counter move.

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:14.450
Every order becomes part of something
the whole community builds together.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:28.950
A campaign like this gives
people a story worth sharing.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.090
We would invite Montreal food creators
and community voices to tell it,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.790
in their own words, if they choose to.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.080
No paid hype.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:41.710
No promise of going viral.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:46.310
Just real people, real
food, and a real goal.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.650
Later, local businesses could join in.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:03.010
Take Kin Academy, as one possible example.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.530
For every qualifying
crash-course registration,

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.910
the partner could fund one shawarma.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:15.300
It's a future idea, subject to approval,
but it shows how the campaign can grow

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.630
beyond one restaurant.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.650
Then comes Christmas week.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:31.570
Verified meal funding
sets the production plan.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.130
The kitchen prepares every meal fresh,
packs it with food-safety controls,

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.630
and coordinates with a confirmed
community organization,

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.930
with distribution targeted
for December twenty-third.

00:03:45.080 --> 00:03:48.110
Afterwards, we report
exactly what was funded,

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:49.950
prepared, and delivered.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.590
For the business, this
is more than goodwill.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.090
Every order is measurable.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.010
Progress gives people something to share.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.330
Sharing builds attention.

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:16.330
Attention can bring partners,
and partners can fund more meals.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:21.110
The possible upside: brand
awareness, earned media,

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.850
community goodwill, and
a stronger identity.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:26.310
None of it is guaranteed.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.890
All of it is worth testing.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.270
One restaurant can start the idea.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.670
An entire community can bring it to life.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.750
Buy one.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.390
Give one.

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:47.260
Spread the mood.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.520
The next step is your
approval: feasibility planning,

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:56.050
budget review, nonprofit outreach,
and campaign development.

